# The same shift register on the ULX3S: its 25 MHz oscillator, and a
# `sys` clock asked for at 125 MHz — five times the input, which an
# `EHXPLLL` makes exactly, with its feedback wired from its own output.
# The request is a `clock_mhz` attribute on the net in the design rather
# than a line here, which is the other way to ask.
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 clk G2
create_clock -name osc -period 40.0 clk
